 "standard_text": "Know and use the function aˣ and its graph; eˣ and ln x; the laws of logarithms; solve equations of the form aˣ = b; use logarithmic graphs to estimate parameters in relationships.",
 "meta_desc": "Free Year 12 A level maths worksheets on exponentials and logarithms: the laws of logarithms, converting between forms, and solving exponential and logarithmic equations. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "log_a x = n means aⁿ = x.",
 "key_sub": "log a + log b = log ab; n log a = log aⁿ.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How it works</h2><p>log<sub>a</sub> <i>x</i> = <i>n</i> means <i>a</i><sup>n</sup> = <i>x</i>. Laws: log <i>a</i> + log <i>b</i> = log <i>ab</i>, log <i>a</i> − log <i>b</i> = log (<i>a</i>/<i>b</i>), <i>k</i> log <i>a</i> = log <i>a</i><sup>k</sup>. ln is the logarithm to base e.</p><p>To solve <i>a</i><sup>x</sup> = <i>b</i>, take logs: <i>x</i> = log <i>b</i> ÷ log <i>a</i>.</p><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Solve 3<sup><i>x</i></sup> = 20.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'><i>x</i> = ln 20 ÷ ln 3</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 2.727 (3 d.p.)</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><ul><li>Writing log(a + b) = log a + log b.</li><li>Dividing the numbers inside the logs instead of the logs.</li><li>Forgetting to check that log equations have positive arguments.</li></ul>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What are the laws of logarithms?",
   "a": "log a + log b = log ab, log a − log b = log(a/b), and k log a = log aᵏ, for the same base."
  },
  {
   "q": "How do you solve aˣ = b?",
   "a": "Take logarithms of both sides: x log a = log b, so x = log b ÷ log a."
  }
 ],
